1
00:00:03,410 --> 00:00:08,410
Hello and welcome to the first of the 12-part series of BioRisk Management.
大家好，欢迎收看生物风险管理 12 集系列讲座的第一讲。

2
00:00:08,410 --> 00:00:12,410
Today's topic is Biological Agents.
今天的主题是生物因子。

3
00:00:12,410 --> 00:00:15,410
This is our schedule for the next 12 months.
这是我们未来 12 个月的安排。

4
00:00:15,410 --> 00:00:24,410
We have designed one lecture module per month in order to disseminate concepts pertaining to biological safety and biological security.
我们设计了每月一个讲座模块，用来传播与生物安全和生物安保相关的概念。

5
00:00:24,410 --> 00:00:34,710
When we are first introduced to BioRisk Management, we have to understand that there are two aspects of BioRisk Management.
初次接触生物风险管理时，我们必须了解生物风险管理包括两个方面。

6
00:00:34,710 --> 00:00:39,710
The first pertains to biosafety and the second pertains to biosecurity.
第一个方面是生物安全，第二个方面是生物安保。

7
00:00:39,710 --> 00:00:43,710
What differentiates these two aspects is the intent.
区分这两个方面的是意图。

8
00:00:43,710 --> 00:00:50,710
So in the case of biosafety, we focus on the unintentional release of biological agents.
对于生物安全，我们关注的是生物因子的非故意释放。

9
00:00:50,710 --> 00:00:57,710
In the case of biosecurity, we focus on the intended release of a biological agent.
对于生物安保，我们关注的是生物因子的蓄意释放。

10
00:00:57,710 --> 00:01:15,020
So throughout this lecture series, we will be focused on the AMP module, which basically pertains to risk assessment, risk mitigation and performance assessment.
在整个系列讲座中，我们将重点讲解 AMP 模块，它基本上包括风险评估、风险缓解和绩效评估。

11
00:01:15,020 --> 00:01:22,020
So these three components are based on continuous quality improvement.
这三个组成部分都建立在持续质量改进的基础之上。

12
00:01:22,020 --> 00:01:26,640
Let's look at biological agents.
我们来看看生物因子。

13
00:01:26,640 --> 00:01:34,640
When we use the term biological agents, we refer to that from the context of biosafety.
我们使用“生物因子”这个术语时，是从生物安全的角度来说的。

14
00:01:34,640 --> 00:01:40,640
However, in the case of biosecurity, we refer to biological agents as biological assets.
而在生物安保中，我们把生物因子称为生物资产。

15
00:01:40,640 --> 00:01:57,630
Some of the keywords we will be using today are index case, morbidity, nosocomial, cutaneous, percutaneous and epidemiology.
今天我们要用到的一些关键词有：指示病例、发病率、医院内的、皮肤的、经皮的以及流行病学。

16
00:01:57,630 --> 00:02:00,630
What is a biological agent?
什么是生物因子？

17
00:02:00,630 --> 00:02:11,630
According to the Occupational Health and Safety Administration, biological agents include bacteria, viruses, fungi, other microorganisms and associated toxins.
根据职业安全与健康管理局的定义，生物因子包括细菌、病毒、真菌、其他微生物以及相关的毒素。

18
00:02:11,630 --> 00:02:22,630
They have the ability to adversely affect human health in a variety of ways, ranging from relatively mild allergic reactions to serious medical conditions or even death.
它们能够以多种方式对人体健康产生不良影响，从相对轻微的过敏反应到严重的疾病，甚至死亡。

19
00:02:22,630 --> 00:02:31,630
Now the key message which we should remember in this definition is that biological agents adversely affect human health.
在这个定义中，我们应该记住的关键信息是：生物因子会对人体健康产生不良影响。

20
00:02:31,630 --> 00:02:37,220
There are various classes of biological agents.
生物因子有多种类别。

21
00:02:37,220 --> 00:02:47,220
One of the least common are prions, which have been linked to what is commonly referred to as the mad cow disease.
最不常见的之一是朊病毒，它与通常所说的疯牛病有关。

22
00:02:47,220 --> 00:02:52,220
So they are a family of progressive neurodegenerative disorders.
它们会引起一类进行性神经退行性疾病。

23
00:02:52,220 --> 00:02:58,220
So prion diseases are spread through animal hosts.
朊病毒病通过动物宿主传播。

24
00:02:58,220 --> 00:03:03,880
The second least common is mycoplasma.
第二不常见的是支原体。

25
00:03:03,880 --> 00:03:07,880
So one of the common biological agents is mycoplasma pneumoniae.
常见的生物因子之一是肺炎支原体。

26
00:03:07,880 --> 00:03:09,880
It's an atypical bacterium.
它是一种非典型细菌。

27
00:03:09,880 --> 00:03:16,880
It does not have a cell wall and does not respond to treatment with beta-lectum antibiotics.
它没有细胞壁，对 β-内酰胺类抗生素治疗无效。

28
00:03:16,880 --> 00:03:19,880
So we need to use macrolides.
所以我们需要使用大环内酯类药物。

29
00:03:19,880 --> 00:03:30,700
So mycoplasma is one of the biological agents, which is atypical, which means it's the only type of bacterium in its class.
所以支原体是一种非典型的生物因子，也就是说，它是同类中唯一的一种细菌。

30
00:03:30,700 --> 00:03:32,700
Viruses are very commonly known.
病毒是大家非常熟悉的。

31
00:03:32,700 --> 00:03:43,700
And the most pathogenic viruses are the positive single-stranded RNA viruses, which include the Ebola virus, the maba virus, and the hunter viruses.
致病性最强的病毒是正链单股 RNA 病毒，其中包括埃博拉病毒、马尔堡病毒和汉坦病毒。

32
00:03:43,700 --> 00:03:47,700
So viruses can cause viral hemorrhagic fevers.
病毒可以引起病毒性出血热。

33
00:03:47,700 --> 00:03:50,700
And these are potentially lethal.
这些疾病可能致命。

34
00:03:50,700 --> 00:03:54,700
And in many cases, treatment for these viruses does not exist.
而且在很多情况下，针对这些病毒的治疗方法并不存在。

35
00:03:54,700 --> 00:03:59,240
Among the bacteria, we have various types of bacteria.
细菌方面，我们有各种类型的细菌。

36
00:03:59,240 --> 00:04:03,240
For instance, we have bacillus anthracis, which is widely known.
例如，有众所周知的炭疽芽孢杆菌。

37
00:04:03,240 --> 00:04:05,240
It's a soil bacterium.
它是一种土壤细菌。

38
00:04:05,240 --> 00:04:12,240
And the production of spores and their dispersals through aerosols is a potential hazard.
它会产生芽孢，芽孢通过气溶胶扩散是一种潜在危害。

39
00:04:12,240 --> 00:04:18,240
We have bulcoidea species, which are found in soils, vibrio and leptospyran.
还有存在于土壤中的伯克霍尔德菌属、弧菌和钩端螺旋体。

40
00:04:18,240 --> 00:04:24,240
These are some of the common bacteria which are associated with biological hazards.
这些是与生物危害相关的一些常见细菌。

41
00:04:24,240 --> 00:04:33,240
Among the yeast, we have yeast such as cryptococcus neiformans, which is an encapsulated yeast, and which is pathogenic,
酵母菌方面，有新型隐球菌这样的酵母菌，它是一种有荚膜的酵母菌，具有致病性，

42
00:04:33,240 --> 00:04:39,160
especially in the case of immunocompromised patients.
特别是对免疫功能低下的患者而言。

43
00:04:39,160 --> 00:04:46,160
In addition to yeast, we also have fungi, which have the ability to be dispersed via spores.
除了酵母菌，还有能够通过孢子传播的真菌。

44
00:04:46,160 --> 00:04:50,160
So aspergillus flavors can cause infection.
黄曲霉可以引起感染。

45
00:04:50,160 --> 00:04:55,160
In fact, aspergillus flavors produces aflatoxin.
事实上，黄曲霉会产生黄曲霉毒素。

46
00:04:55,160 --> 00:05:02,160
We have histoplasma, which is spread by guano, or in the feces of birds, and candida albicans,
还有通过鸟粪，也就是鸟类粪便传播的组织胞浆菌，以及白色念珠菌，

47
00:05:02,160 --> 00:05:05,160
which is a common cell yeast.
它是一种常见的共生酵母菌。

48
00:05:05,160 --> 00:05:11,160
However, in immunocompromised patients, it can manifest as an infection.
但在免疫功能低下的患者中，它可能表现为感染。

49
00:05:11,160 --> 00:05:16,160
In addition to this, caution should be taken when working with DNA and RNA,
此外，在处理 DNA 和 RNA 时也应谨慎，

50
00:05:16,160 --> 00:05:20,160
because DNA and RNA represent potential infectious agents.
因为 DNA 和 RNA 是潜在的感染因子。

51
00:05:20,160 --> 00:05:28,370
As has been reported in a paper, novel virus RNA is infectious in mammalian cells.
正如一篇论文所报道的，某种新型病毒的 RNA 在哺乳动物细胞中具有感染性。

52
00:05:28,370 --> 00:05:37,370
In addition to the naturally occurring infectious agents, genetically modified infectious agents represent a threat as well.
除了自然存在的感染因子，经过基因改造的感染因子也构成威胁。

53
00:05:37,370 --> 00:05:42,370
Modifications which increase virulence, expand the host range,
那些增强毒力、扩大宿主范围、

54
00:05:42,370 --> 00:05:47,370
improve the resistance, or increase resistance to therapeutic agents, such as antibiotics,
提高抗性或增强对抗生素等治疗药物的耐药性、

55
00:05:47,370 --> 00:05:52,370
and which mask their antigens from host immune system.
以及使其抗原躲避宿主免疫系统的改造。

56
00:05:52,370 --> 00:05:59,370
All these modifications can lead to a potential biological threat.
所有这些改造都可能导致潜在的生物威胁。

57
00:05:59,370 --> 00:06:03,370
In addition to this, we have other parasites, like backbone parasites,
此外，还有其他寄生虫，比如媒介传播的寄生虫，

58
00:06:03,370 --> 00:06:09,370
such as those spread by the Aedes aegypti,
例如由埃及伊蚊传播的寄生虫，

59
00:06:09,370 --> 00:06:15,370
as well as schistosoma, which is spread by aquatic snails.
以及由水生螺类传播的血吸虫。

60
00:06:15,370 --> 00:06:20,370
We have ticks and fleas, which can serve as vectors for the transmission of bacterial pathogens,
还有蜱和跳蚤，它们可以作为传播细菌性病原体的媒介，

61
00:06:20,370 --> 00:06:24,370
as well as ricin and other biologically derived toxins,
以及蓖麻毒素和其他生物来源的毒素，

62
00:06:24,370 --> 00:06:28,370
which have the potential to cause harm even though they are non-living.
它们虽然不是活体，但也有可能造成伤害。

63
00:06:28,370 --> 00:06:36,450
So, we have a wide range of biological agents. How are they classified?
所以，生物因子的范围很广。它们是如何分类的呢？

64
00:06:36,450 --> 00:06:40,450
Biological agents are classified according to their risk group.
生物因子是按照风险等级组来分类的。

65
00:06:40,450 --> 00:06:45,450
Risk group 1 do not cause diseases in healthy adult humans.
风险等级 1 组不会使健康的成年人致病。

66
00:06:45,450 --> 00:06:51,450
Lactobacillus, Lactis is a perfect example, it's a probiotic, it causes no harm.
乳酸乳杆菌就是一个很好的例子，它是一种益生菌，不会造成任何伤害。

67
00:06:51,450 --> 00:06:57,760
Risk group 2 cause disease in humans, but the disease is treatable or preventable.
风险等级 2 组会使人致病，但这种疾病是可以治疗或预防的。

68
00:06:58,760 --> 00:07:02,760
Therapies exist and the treatment protocols are well-defined.
有现成的疗法，而且治疗方案明确。

69
00:07:02,760 --> 00:07:08,420
Risk group 3 organisms can cause serious diseases in humans.
风险等级 3 组的生物体可以使人患上严重疾病。

70
00:07:08,420 --> 00:07:11,420
You can have mortality as well as morbidity.
可能导致死亡，也可能导致发病。

71
00:07:11,420 --> 00:07:16,420
However, treatment exists and vaccines for the diseases have been developed.
不过，有治疗方法，而且针对这些疾病的疫苗也已研制出来。

72
00:07:16,420 --> 00:07:23,090
In the case of risk group 4, for example, in the Simeon herpes virus,
至于风险等级 4 组，例如猴疱疹病毒，

73
00:07:23,090 --> 00:07:30,090
they cause deadly disease and there is no treatment or vaccine available for this kind of pathogen.
它们会引起致命疾病，而且对这类病原体没有可用的治疗方法或疫苗。

74
00:07:30,090 --> 00:07:36,460
One of the widely used references is the pathogen safety data sheet.
广泛使用的参考资料之一是病原体安全数据表。

75
00:07:36,460 --> 00:07:41,460
These pathogen safety data sheets have been developed by the Public Health Agency of Canada
这些病原体安全数据表由加拿大公共卫生署编制，

76
00:07:41,460 --> 00:07:47,460
and they give an overview of the risk group as well as the therapeutic procedures
概述了病原体的风险等级组，以及临床医生

77
00:07:47,460 --> 00:07:51,460
which can be adopted by a clinician in the case of infection.
在发生感染时可以采用的治疗方法。

78
00:07:51,460 --> 00:07:56,120
Now, we work in a laboratory setting.
我们是在实验室环境中工作的。

79
00:07:56,120 --> 00:08:01,120
So, what increases the level of risk is the processing of samples.
所以，增加风险水平的是样本的处理。

80
00:08:01,120 --> 00:08:06,120
For instance, in this case, you can see that storage does not pose a significant risk
例如，在这个例子中，大家可以看到储存并不构成重大风险，

81
00:08:06,120 --> 00:08:13,120
because in a stored state, the bacterium or the biological agent is in a dormant state.
因为在储存状态下，细菌或者说生物因子处于休眠状态。

82
00:08:13,120 --> 00:08:17,120
However, when this bacterium is thawed and brought into the lab for diagnosis,
然而，当这种细菌被解冻并带进实验室进行诊断时，

83
00:08:17,120 --> 00:08:21,120
it poses a risk to the environment as well as to the laboratory worker.
它就会对环境和实验室工作人员构成风险。

84
00:08:21,120 --> 00:08:29,120
When this organism is cultured, for instance, for development of vaccines or attenuated viruses,
当这种生物体被培养时，例如用于研制疫苗或减毒病毒，

85
00:08:29,120 --> 00:08:37,120
they can pose a risk to the larger context which means the laboratory worker as well as the environment.
它们可能会在更大范围内构成风险，也就是对实验室工作人员和环境都构成风险。

86
00:08:37,120 --> 00:08:46,120
So, as you can see in this depiction, the modification of viruses or the application of technologies
所以，正如大家在这张示意图中看到的，对病毒进行改造，或者应用各种技术

87
00:08:46,120 --> 00:08:54,120
to process risk groups or in this case, viruses can lead to greater levels of risk
来处理各风险等级组的生物因子，在这里是病毒，都可能导致更高的风险水平，

88
00:08:54,120 --> 00:09:00,010
and these need to be taken into account when you are working in a laboratory setting.
在实验室环境中工作时必须考虑到这些。

89
00:09:00,010 --> 00:09:04,010
So, we will be discussing risk in more detail in future lectures.
我们将在以后的讲座中更详细地讨论风险。

90
00:09:04,010 --> 00:09:10,010
But just to touch upon risk, risk is a function of likelihood and consequence.
这里只简单提一下，风险是可能性和后果的函数。

91
00:09:10,010 --> 00:09:16,010
When we speak of likelihood, we ask the question, what is the probability of?
谈到可能性时，我们问的问题是：发生……的概率是多少？

92
00:09:16,010 --> 00:09:21,010
When we speak of consequence, we ask the question, what would happen if?
谈到后果时，我们问的问题是：如果……会发生什么？

93
00:09:21,010 --> 00:09:26,580
So, this is a risk matrix which defines likelihood and consequence.
这是一个定义可能性和后果的风险矩阵。

94
00:09:26,580 --> 00:09:32,580
So, a risk with a likelihood and consequence of 1 and 1 represents a low risk.
可能性和后果分别为 1 和 1 的风险，代表低风险。

95
00:09:32,580 --> 00:09:38,580
A risk with a likelihood and consequence of 5 and 5 represents a high risk.
可能性和后果分别为 5 和 5 的风险，代表高风险。

96
00:09:38,580 --> 00:09:42,580
Now, this is an indicator matrix which can be used for risk assessment.
这是一个可用于风险评估的指示矩阵。

97
00:09:42,580 --> 00:09:45,580
So, how do we assess risk?
那么，我们如何评估风险呢？

98
00:09:45,580 --> 00:09:49,580
What are the questions that we need to ask when we assess risk?
评估风险时，我们需要提出哪些问题？

99
00:09:49,580 --> 00:09:55,240
The first question which we need to ask is the risk group.
我们需要问的第一个问题是风险等级组。

100
00:09:55,240 --> 00:10:01,240
Which risk group does my biological agent belong to?
我的生物因子属于哪个风险等级组？

101
00:10:01,240 --> 00:10:04,240
Which risk group can it be assigned to?
可以把它划入哪个风险等级组？

102
00:10:04,240 --> 00:10:07,240
The second question is the root of infection.
第二个问题是感染途径。

103
00:10:07,240 --> 00:10:12,240
Do we get infected by inhalation, aerosols?
我们是通过吸入、气溶胶而被感染的吗？

104
00:10:12,240 --> 00:10:17,240
Do we get infected by a contact which is percutaneous and cutaneous?
是通过经皮和皮肤的接触而被感染的吗？

105
00:10:17,240 --> 00:10:21,240
Do we get infected by an injection which is percutaneous?
是通过经皮的注射而被感染的吗？

106
00:10:21,240 --> 00:10:24,240
Or do we get infected by an injection?
还是通过食入而被感染的？

107
00:10:24,240 --> 00:10:30,830
The second aspect which we need to address is the mode of transmission.
我们需要关注的第二个方面是传播方式。

108
00:10:30,830 --> 00:10:36,830
If a vector is involved in the transmission of a virus from one human host to another,
如果病毒从一个人类宿主传播到另一个人类宿主的过程中涉及媒介，

109
00:10:36,830 --> 00:10:42,830
does this virus get transmitted directly as in the case of the Zika virus?
这种病毒是像寨卡病毒那样直接传播的吗？

110
00:10:42,830 --> 00:10:51,830
Or does it have to go through the host life cycle as in the case of the Aedes aegypti carrying virus?
还是必须像埃及伊蚊携带的病毒那样，经过宿主的生命周期？

111
00:10:51,830 --> 00:10:59,390
Some of the host may be diverse.
有些宿主可能是多种多样的。

112
00:10:59,390 --> 00:11:03,390
For instance, Cryptococcus is actually present in plants,
例如，隐球菌实际上存在于植物中，

113
00:11:03,390 --> 00:11:06,390
spread by spores and infects humans.
通过孢子传播并感染人类。

114
00:11:06,390 --> 00:11:10,390
But it's also present in bird excreta or in bird droppings.
但它也存在于鸟类排泄物，也就是鸟粪中。

115
00:11:10,390 --> 00:11:15,390
And these can be vectors for the transmission of this specific pathogen.
这些都可能成为传播这种特定病原体的媒介。

116
00:11:15,390 --> 00:11:24,560
In addition to the root of transmission, we also have to look at the host range.
除了传播途径，我们还要看宿主范围。

117
00:11:24,560 --> 00:11:28,560
Some viruses can survive and propagate in multiple series of host.
有些病毒可以在多种宿主中存活和繁殖。

118
00:11:28,560 --> 00:11:33,560
They can propagate in mammals as well as in snails.
它们既可以在哺乳动物体内繁殖，也可以在螺类体内繁殖。

119
00:11:33,560 --> 00:11:40,900
So we need to consider this aspect when we develop a bioresk management plan.
所以在制定生物风险管理计划时，我们需要考虑这一点。

120
00:11:40,900 --> 00:11:42,900
The next question is infectious dose.
下一个问题是感染剂量。

121
00:11:42,900 --> 00:11:47,900
How much of the biological agent is required in order to cause harm?
需要多少生物因子才能造成伤害？

122
00:11:47,900 --> 00:11:50,900
In this case, morbidity or mortality.
在这里，伤害指的是发病或死亡。

123
00:11:50,900 --> 00:11:55,690
The next aspect is endemicity.
下一个方面是地方流行性。

124
00:11:55,690 --> 00:12:00,690
Is the biological agent endemic to this specific region?
这种生物因子在这个特定地区是否属于地方性流行？

125
00:12:00,690 --> 00:12:05,690
So if a biological agent is endemic to a specific region,
如果一种生物因子在某个特定地区，

126
00:12:05,690 --> 00:12:08,690
a geographic region in this case,
这里指的是某个地理区域，属于地方性流行，

127
00:12:08,690 --> 00:12:12,690
it is likely that individuals who are endemic to that region
那么这个地区的本地居民

128
00:12:12,690 --> 00:12:16,690
have developed some level of immunity to this biological agent.
很可能已经对这种生物因子产生了一定程度的免疫力。

129
00:12:16,690 --> 00:12:23,320
In addition to this, we need to look at the immune status of the laboratory worker.
此外，我们还需要了解实验室工作人员的免疫状况。

130
00:12:23,320 --> 00:12:26,320
Is the laboratory worker immunocompromised?
实验室工作人员是否免疫功能低下？

131
00:12:26,320 --> 00:12:28,320
So if they are immunocompromised,
如果他们免疫功能低下，

132
00:12:28,320 --> 00:12:33,320
we need to put in place measures to mitigate the risk posed to this laboratory worker.
我们就需要采取措施，降低这名实验室工作人员面临的风险。

133
00:12:33,320 --> 00:12:38,050
So finally, we come down to the risk assessment,
最后，我们来到风险评估，

134
00:12:38,050 --> 00:12:42,050
which is basically a series of questions which we ask.
它基本上就是我们要问的一系列问题。

135
00:12:42,050 --> 00:12:45,050
What is the biological agent?
这是什么生物因子？

136
00:12:45,050 --> 00:12:47,050
What is the risk group which can be assigned to?
可以把它划入哪个风险等级组？

137
00:12:47,050 --> 00:12:50,050
Is it endemic or exotic?
它是本地流行的还是外来的？

138
00:12:50,050 --> 00:12:52,050
Which risk group can it be assigned to?
可以把它划入哪个风险等级组？

139
00:12:52,050 --> 00:12:54,050
What is the mode of transmission?
传播方式是什么？

140
00:12:54,050 --> 00:12:56,050
What is the root of infection?
感染途径是什么？

141
00:12:56,050 --> 00:12:58,050
What is the infectious dose?
感染剂量是多少？

142
00:12:58,050 --> 00:13:01,050
And is treatment available?
是否有治疗方法？

143
00:13:01,050 --> 00:13:04,050
When we do risk assessment in the laboratory,
在实验室中进行风险评估时，

144
00:13:04,050 --> 00:13:07,050
these are some of the questions which we need to ask.
这些是我们需要问的一些问题。

145
00:13:07,050 --> 00:13:11,050
What is the immune status of the laboratory workers?
实验室工作人员的免疫状况如何？

146
00:13:11,050 --> 00:13:14,050
What are the processes that will be employed in the laboratory workers
实验室工作人员将采用哪些操作过程，

147
00:13:14,050 --> 00:13:20,050
as well as the volume of the culture which is going to be processed?
以及要处理的培养物的体积有多大？

148
00:13:20,050 --> 00:13:22,050
How many processes are involved?
涉及多少个操作过程？

149
00:13:23,050 --> 00:13:25,050
Does the laboratory work involve a single step
实验室工作是只涉及单一步骤，

150
00:13:25,050 --> 00:13:28,050
or does it encompass multiple steps?
还是包含多个步骤？

151
00:13:28,050 --> 00:13:31,050
How many workers are exposed?
有多少工作人员会受到暴露？

152
00:13:31,050 --> 00:13:33,050
Have they been trained?
他们是否接受过培训？

153
00:13:33,050 --> 00:13:36,050
And has the facility been designed for a specific purpose?
设施是否是为特定用途而设计的？

154
00:13:36,050 --> 00:13:40,860
When we do risk assessment,
进行风险评估时，

155
00:13:40,860 --> 00:13:44,860
we always address the iceberg analogy
我们总是会提到冰山的比喻，

156
00:13:44,860 --> 00:13:51,860
in which case a large portion of the risk is actually present but not visible
也就是说，很大一部分风险实际上是存在的，但是看不见，

157
00:13:51,860 --> 00:13:56,860
and you may not be able to assess this risk
而且你可能无法用传统的方法或传统的问题

158
00:13:56,860 --> 00:13:59,860
using traditional approaches or traditional questions
来评估这部分风险，

159
00:13:59,860 --> 00:14:03,860
because there is no knowledge pertaining to previous cases.
因为没有以往病例的相关知识。

160
00:14:03,860 --> 00:14:06,860
We can only see the risk which is visible
我们只能看到那些可见的风险，

161
00:14:06,860 --> 00:14:12,300
or which appears as a result of specific questions.
或者通过特定问题显现出来的风险。

162
00:14:12,300 --> 00:14:16,300
So in this case, we assume the highest level of risk.
所以在这种情况下，我们假定风险处于最高水平。

163
00:14:16,300 --> 00:14:19,300
So pertaining to the iceberg analogy,
所以，根据冰山的比喻，

164
00:14:19,300 --> 00:14:21,300
we always assume the highest level of risk
对于以下情况，我们总是假定风险处于最高水平：

165
00:14:21,300 --> 00:14:23,300
in the case of genetically engineered molecules,
基因工程分子，

166
00:14:23,300 --> 00:14:25,300
be it RNA or DNA.
无论是 RNA 还是 DNA；

167
00:14:25,300 --> 00:14:28,300
Rosocomial samples which may contain a multiplicity
可能含有多种生物因子或病原体的

168
00:14:28,300 --> 00:14:30,300
of biological agents or pathogens.
医院内样本；

169
00:14:30,300 --> 00:14:35,300
Soil samples which may lead to potential sporulation
可能导致潜在孢子形成，

170
00:14:35,300 --> 00:14:40,300
or which may lead to the development of bacteria or fungi with spores.
或者可能导致产孢细菌或真菌生长的土壤样本；

171
00:14:40,300 --> 00:14:43,300
Samples run from healthy organisms
取自健康生物体的样本，

172
00:14:43,300 --> 00:14:47,300
which may not present the symptoms of infection.
它们可能不表现出感染症状，

173
00:14:47,300 --> 00:14:51,300
However, which may be a host for that specific pathogen.
但可能是该特定病原体的宿主；

174
00:14:51,300 --> 00:14:54,300
And samples derived from vile animals.
以及取自野生动物的样本。

175
00:14:54,300 --> 00:15:01,510
So once we address or assess the risk,
所以，一旦我们处理或评估了风险，

176
00:15:01,510 --> 00:15:05,510
we then mitigate the risk by the application of five controls
就要通过实施五种控制措施来缓解风险，

177
00:15:05,510 --> 00:15:09,510
which are elimination, substitution, engineering controls,
即消除、替代、工程控制、

178
00:15:09,510 --> 00:15:14,510
administrative controls and personal protective equipment.
管理控制和个人防护装备。

179
00:15:14,510 --> 00:15:16,510
Once we have applied the control,
实施了控制措施之后，

180
00:15:16,510 --> 00:15:19,510
we assess the performance of our controls
我们要通过对操作过程

181
00:15:19,510 --> 00:15:21,510
by carrying out an audit of the processes
和标准操作规程进行审核，

182
00:15:21,510 --> 00:15:26,510
and the standard operating procedures.
来评估控制措施的效果。

183
00:15:26,510 --> 00:15:28,510
These are some of the references
这些是制作本讲解时

184
00:15:28,510 --> 00:15:33,510
which have been relied upon to develop this presentation.
所依据的一些参考资料。

185
00:15:33,510 --> 00:15:39,180
Our next module will focus on risk assessment.
我们的下一个模块将重点讲解风险评估。

186
00:15:39,180 --> 00:15:44,180
Thank you for participating in this BiRisk Management Series.
感谢大家参与本生物风险管理系列讲座。
